\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Fixed connections and dynamical fields}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{A connection in this chapter is fixed background data. Gauge
transformations compare its descriptions; taking their quotient does
not prescribe a probability law on connections. The
[holonomy action](fdip-006I) integrates matter while retaining the
connection as a parameter. To make the connection dynamical one must
also specify its integration measure and action, and then integrate
or sum over connection configurations.}

\p{The earlier [induced action on weighted graphs](fdip-005Q) likewise
keeps the weights fixed. One could subsequently promote them to
integration variables, but that is an additional model choice. Neither
the fixed-weight action nor the present connection construction makes
weights dynamical or supplies gravitational dynamics. A prescribed
circle limit and a twisted spatial Dirac operator also do not supply
a time direction, reflection positivity or Lorentzian reconstruction.
These distinctions remain part of the
[open physical interfaces](fdip-003Y).}
